# Adjudicated `punused` findings for web-terminal-kiro. One reason per entry;
# entries match as literal substrings of the finding line, so never include
# file:line:col — line numbers shift and the entry silently goes stale.

# --- Startup-failure stage attribution (main.go).
#
# Unwrap is called by the standard library, never by name from this repo:
# `errors.As`/`errors.Is` walk a chain by type-asserting to `interface{ Unwrap()
# error }`, so no call site exists for punused to find. Deleting it would not
# fail the build — it would silently break the chain, which is why the
# attribution's own test asserts `errors.Is` still reaches the cause
# (TestAtStagePreservesTheMessageAndTheChain). The method is load-bearing and
# permanently call-site-free.
method (*stageError).Unwrap


# --- Workflow-mark watcher (workflowmark.go): staged behind an unreleased engine
# API, so its entry point has no production caller YET.
#
# Run is the poller's goroutine entry, the shape sessionTitleSync.Run already
# has. What is missing is the join: main.go can only construct the watcher and
# pass its reading to terminal.NewSessionManager once the engine publishes
# WithSessionActivity and go.mod picks that release up. Until then the type is
# exercised by its tests alone, which is what punused reports.
#
# DELETE this entry in the same commit that wires the watcher up. It is the only
# thing keeping the gap visible, so leaving it behind would hide a watcher that
# silently never runs.
method (*workflowWatch).Run
